{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785236471,"nonce":"8yaYQQ/MR9aMJbRD6DhONM4sBaI=","title":"ADR-0062: the Export ladder omits a reflink rung the Farm ladder already has","message":"ADR-0062's two ladders are asymmetric in a way that looks unintentional. The **Farm** ladder's top rung is `reflink` (`FICLONE`/`clonefile`) — a local metadata operation in the tens of microseconds, no bytes moved. The **Export** ladder has only two rungs: `overlayfs` with the Farm as lowerdir (needs `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`), and \"a writable copy of the Farm\" (needs nothing).\n\nBut a Farm and its Exports live on **one filesystem** — `SnapshotFarm::new` puts farms under `\u003cwarm_dir\u003e/farms` precisely so a reflink cannot cross a filesystem boundary. So \"a writable copy of the Farm\" could be a **CoW clone of the Farm**, which is:\n\n- nearly free, where the Farm's own reflink rung is available;\n- **correct**, because copy-on-write independence is exactly what a reflink gives — a write to the clone does not touch the Farm, which is the same property the overlay rung relies on;\n- metadata-exact per entry, unlike a hardlink (the reason the Farm cannot use hardlinks at all).\n\nThat would make the unprivileged Export rung nearly as cheap as the privileged one on any reflink-capable filesystem, which materially weakens the argument that `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` is the *preferred* configuration. The change set would still be the `(size, mtime, ctime)` stat-cache approximation rather than exact — that difference is unaffected and remains the real reason to prefer the overlay.\n\nFound while implementing s4's Export rungs (`crates/scarab-server/src/export.rs`). Not built: `farm::reflink` is private to `farm.rs`.\n\n- [ ] Make `farm::reflink` reachable (`pub(crate)`) or expose a Farm-cloning operation on `SnapshotFarm`\n- [ ] Add the rung, and have it report itself — ADR-0062 requires every build to state which rung it took, and this makes three\n- [ ] Measure the clone rung against the copy rung for a realistic tree, stating the filesystem; the dogfood disk is ext4 and has no reflink, so it cannot exercise this rung at all\n- [ ] Amend ADR-0062's Export-ladder table and its \"what refusing the capability actually costs\" paragraph","files":null}]}